{
  "name": "rest_easy",
  "description": "A legacy Rust compiler plugin that implements a custom lint to signal the transition from static analysis to the code generation phase. By hooking into the crate validation pass, it notifies the developer once the compiler has completed all checks that could result in a compilation error, indicating that the remaining build time is dedicated to translation. This provides an early success signal for long-running builds before the computationally intensive codegen process begins.",
